This repository contains the software project for the {{ title|default(name) }} Drupal website. It contains a Drupal installation with custom business logic, configuration, themes and styling for the website.

* [Live URL]({{ url }}/)
* [Local URL](https://{{ name }}.ddev.site/)


## Prerequisites

- **WSL2**: For usage with Windows it is required to use WSL2.
- **Docker**: Required if you wish to use the integrated development environment.
- **DDEV**: Make sure you have [ddev](https://ddev.readthedocs.io/) installed on your system.
- **VS Code**: Recommended for developing code with the provided settings and extensions.
- **Git Access**: To clone the repository and manage version control.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> _Make sure to install the right version of DDEV for your system. We recommend DDEV on Windows with WSL2 + Docker Desktop ([docs](https://ddev.readthedocs.io/en/stable/users/install/ddev-installation/#windows)). Additionally it is required to set up SSH authentication in DDEV so Drush can access the remote environment using `ddev auth ssh -f $HOME/.ssh/YOUR_SSH_KEY`._

## Quick Start

1. **Clone the Repository**:
   Clone the repository from GitHub to your local machine.

2. **Install the Project**:
   ```bash
   make install
   ```
   Starts the DDEV runtimes, builds and deploys Drupal. For development this can also be skipped and executed in VS Code.

3. **Launch the Project**:
   ```bash
   make launch
   ```
   Opens up your browser on the project's homepage. To directly log into the admin backend, use `make login`.

## Local Development

To start developing locally, you can launch a Visual Studio Code environment customized for this project by running:

```bash
make code
```
This will open VS Code configured to work with your local environment.

### Useful Commands

* `make install`: Install the project with runtime locally.
   > Use `DDEV_SNAPSHOT=latest` flag to restore the latest `ddev` snapshot.
* `make code`: Start a VS Code dev environment.
* `make drupal`: Build & deploy Drupal backend locally. Runs daemonized.
* `make test`: Run project tests (PHPUnit, …).
* `make lint`: Lint the project (PHPCS, …).
* `make beauty`: Beautify & fix code in project.

> [!TIP]
> _Run `make help` for a list of all available commands. Some commands are also available as tasks in VS Code._

> [!TIP]
> _Use `ddev snapshot` to take database snapshots and run `make install DDEV_SNAPSHOT=latest` to re-install from the latest database snapshots (named snapshots are supported)._

